    "bio": "a Representative from Pennsylvania; born in Glassport, Allegheny County, Pa., January 23, 1932; B.S., University of Pittsburgh, Pa., 1954; M.B.A., Duquesne University, Pittsburgh, Pa., 1960; Ph.D., American University, Washington, D.C., 1967; United States Army, 1954-1956; business owner; delegate, Republican National Conventions, 1976, 1980, 1984, and 1988; elected as a Republican to the Ninety-third and to the fourteen succeeding Congresses, served until his resignation on February 3, 2001 (January 3, 1973-February 3, 2001); chairman, Committee on Transportation and Infrastructure (One Hundred Fourth through One Hundred Sixth Congresses); died on April 19, 2023, in Everett, Pa.",
